Cell[TextData[{
 "\nWhen might it be ",
 StyleBox["necessary",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " to require assignment by using the 2nd argument?\nExample: If you want to \
compare the incoming value # to the outgoing value f.\nThe 2nd argument of \
Dynamic plots # and f first and then assigns f=# second.\nOnce the assignment \
has been made, the old value is gone.\nI do not know any other way to do this \
using only one argument in Dynamic except to use the 2nd argument of Dynamic.\
\nClick the following popup several times:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.391202712942*^9, 3.391202821877*^9}, {3.391203170322*^9,
    3.391203193859*^9}, {3.3912044355369997`*^9, 3.391204482233*^9}, {
